#> tool: awkrepl
#> wait: Beth appears 2 times
#> pause: 30
#> must: Beth appears 2 times
#> not: Beth appears 0 times
#> source: appears
# 7. Count the lines that contain "Beth". Pement: awk '/Beth/{n++}; END {print n+0}'
# A regex pattern selects lines; n++ counts them. n+0 turns an unset n into 0
# instead of printing an empty string when there are no matches.
# Try: change the regex to /Mar/ (matches Mark and Mary) and predict the count.
/Beth/ { n++ }
END { print "Beth appears " n+0 " times" }

#DATA
Beth    4.00  0
Dan     3.75  0
Kathy   4.00  10

Mark    5.00  20
Mary    5.50  22
Susie   4.25  18
Susie   4.25  18
Beth    4.00  0

Kathy   4.00  10
